{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf48VDHAY19je36zP3XhX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the current state of the rate-limit initiative. I read it only — nothing was gated, stamped, run, or accepted.\n\n## Initiative: `rate-limit` (intent `DI-RATE-LIMIT`)\n\nGraph digest `sha256:346db4bd…` — **4 tasks, 1 ready, 0 issues**.\n\n| Task | Effort | Depends on | Status | Sealed? | Accepted? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `T-20260802-policy-schema` — Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema | S | — | ready (unblocked) | no | no |\n| `T-20260802-effective-policy` — Resolve one effective organization policy | S | policy-schema | ready, **blocked** | no | no |\n| `T-20260802-request-101` — Enforce the effective limit at request 101 | S | effective-policy | ready, **blocked** | no | no |\n| `T-20260802-decision-visibility` — Expose denial reason and decision telemetry | S | request-101 | ready, **blocked** | no | no |\n\nAll four are `authorization=Tier-3`, `signed_off: false`, `accepted: false`. The chain is strictly linear: schema → policy resolution → enforcement → visibility. Only `policy-schema` has met dependencies; concurrency groups confirm one lane (`[[\"T-20260802-policy-schema\"]]`).\n\n## Where the work stands in the lifecycle\n\n**Planned and reviewed, not authorized.** The decomposition is complete and the plan review is signed:\n\n- `reviews/delivery-plan-review.json` — disposition `accepted`, reviewer `fixture-controller`, reviewed 2026-09-14, HMAC `hmac-taskplan-v1:792a1744…`, over plan `50c9032b…` and topology `e1743daa…`.\n- Lineage (`task-plan-lineage.json`) maps each task to its leg, seam, and swimlane, all under TaskPlan digest `0b324272…`.\n- The review's own reason states it plainly: *\"Explicit synthetic topology fixture for authorized chat qualification; **no leaf execution authorization**.\"*\n\nTelemetry backs that up — `telemetry/events.jsonl` holds exactly three events (`decompose.recipe`, `decompose.plan`, `decompose.review`), every one with `authorization: false`. There are no gate, run, or acceptance events, no `.taskspec` mesh runtime state, and no source files exist yet at the declared `creates_paths` (`src/rate_limit/…`).\n\nSo: a plan review is not a leaf seal. These four leaves are unsealed, and nothing has executed.\n\n## On the tool's suggested next step\n\n`taskspec status` prints a `NEXT=taskspec gate --stamp …` line for each task. I did not run it and am not proposing it — `gate` executes task evals, and `--stamp` writes the sign-off envelope that authorizes that exact revision. That's the authorization boundary you told me to leave alone.\n\nRead-only inspection remains available if useful: `taskspec graph`, `taskspec status <task>`, `taskspec plan`, `taskspec recipe`, and `taskspec dod`. Note that `gate` and `accept` execute evals even without `--stamp`, so they aren't status queries; I'd need your explicit go-ahead for either.\n\nOne note for later: the repo pins the CLI at `/private/tmp/taskspec-chat-effects-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec`, and the `taskspec` on `PATH` is 3.9.0. I used the pinned 3.10.0 binary throughout, which matches the engine version recorded in the lineage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":24465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":970},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e0fd51d6-3068-462b-91d6-9033f2a38296","uuid":"a46467a7-acba-48cf-af94-041fe8b16a45","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:35:38.854Z","request_id":"req_011Cf48VChgczY8FLcPgDzuC"}
